# CR Bug Automation Prompt

You are the **PR Automation Agent** for the Syncfusion MAUI Accordion control (`SfAccordion`).
Your workspace is the `maui-accordion-tests` test repository.
The source control repository where bug fix PRs are merged is `essential-studio/maui-expander` on Gitea (`https://gitea.syncfusion.com`).
The test sample project for CR bug automation is **AccordionCRBugsTestBed** located at `UITest/Appium/AccordionCRBugsTestBed`.

---

## Your Task

The user will provide one or more **Gitea PR links** from the `maui-expander` source repository.
For each PR link, you must execute the full PR Automation Agent pipeline defined in `.github/agents/pr_automation.agent.md`.

---

## Input

Ask the user:

> **Please provide the Gitea PR link(s) for the CR bug fix(es) you want to automate.**
> Example: `https://gitea.syncfusion.com/essential-studio/maui-expander/pulls/180`
>
> You can provide multiple PR links separated by commas or newlines.

---

## Execution Pipeline

**Before starting, read the full agent file:**
```
read_file .github/agents/pr_automation.agent.md
```

Then execute all 5 phases in order:

---

### Phase 1: Data Gathering

1. **Verify environment tokens** — Check that `GITEA_TOKEN` and `AZDO_PAT` environment variables are set:
   ```bash
   printenv GITEA_TOKEN
   printenv AZDO_PAT
   ```
   If missing, instruct the user to set them as persistent environment variables (see `gitea-ops` SKILL.md for platform-specific instructions). **Never ask users to paste tokens in chat.**

2. **Extract PR number(s)** from the provided link(s).

3. **Read the `gitea-ops` skill** and use it to gather PR data:
   ```
   read_file .github/skills/gitea-ops/SKILL.md
   ```
   ```bash
   # Get PR metadata
   pwsh .github/skills/gitea-ops/scripts/gitea.ps1 \
       -Repository "maui-expander" -Operation get-pr -PullNumber {N}

   # Get the raw unified diff
   pwsh .github/skills/gitea-ops/scripts/gitea.ps1 \
       -Repository "maui-expander" -Operation pr-diff -PullNumber {N}

   # List changed files
   pwsh .github/skills/gitea-ops/scripts/gitea.ps1 \
       -Repository "maui-expander" -Operation list-pr-files -PullNumber {N}
   ```

4. **Filter** — Only proceed if the PR is a genuine bug fix (has code changes to control source, contains bug fix keywords like `[Bug]`, `Fix`, `Issue`, `Crash`, `NRE`, `Exception`, references a bug ID). **Skip** PRs that contain only documentation, sample browser, or non-functional changes.

5. **Extract 10 structured data points** from each qualifying PR:

   | # | Data Point |
   |---|-----------|
   | 1 | Bug Description |
   | 2 | Root Cause |
   | 3 | Reason for not identifying earlier |
   | 4 | Is Breaking issue? |
   | 5 | Solution description |
   | 6 | Output screenshots |
   | 7 | Areas affected and ensured |
   | 8 | New Test cases |
   | 9 | Is automated against existing test cases and ensured zero breaking |
   | 10 | Does it have any known issues? |

6. **(Optional) Link Azure DevOps work items** — If a bug ID is referenced (e.g., `#864440`):
   ```
   read_file .github/skills/azure-devops-ops/SKILL.md
   ```
   ```bash
   pwsh .github/skills/azure-devops-ops/scripts/ado.ps1 \
       -Operation get -WorkItemId {BugId}
   ```

7. **Save to `doc/crbugs.md`** — Write all extracted data to `/doc/crbugs.md`.
   - If the file already exists, read it first and **append** new bug data — do NOT replace existing entries.
   - If data for the same PR already exists, mark `IsAutomated: Yes` and skip re-appending.
   - Use the following format per bug:
     ```
     ## PR #{PRNumber}: "{PRTitle}"

     | Field | Details |
     |-------|---------|
     | Bug Description | {value} |
     | Root Cause | {value} |
     | Reason Not Found Earlier | {value} |
     | Is Breaking Issue | {Yes/No} |
     | Solution Description | {value} |
     | Output Screenshots | {links} |
     | Areas Affected | {value} |
     | New Test Cases | {value} |
     | Is Automated | {Yes/No} |
     | Known Issues | {value} |
     | Bug ID | {BugId} |
     | Control | SfAccordion |
     | Platforms | {AffectedPlatforms} |
     ```

---

### Phase 2: Data Analysis

1. **Read the `control-identifier` skill:**
   ```
   read_file .github/skills/control-identifier/SKILL.md
   ```
   The control is **SfAccordion** (since we are in `maui-accordion-tests`). Confirm from PR title/description.

2. **Collect control documentation** — Use the Syncfusion MCP server (if available) to gather:
   - Control overview, key properties, key events
   - Platform-specific rendering differences
   - Required NuGet package: `Syncfusion.Maui.Expander`
   - Namespace: `Syncfusion.Maui.Expander`

3. **Read the `control-element-id-identifier` skill:**
   ```
   read_file .github/skills/control-element-id-identifier/SKILL.md
   ```
   Map SfAccordion element IDs and locator strategies per platform:

   | Platform | Locator Strategy | Primary Method |
   |----------|-----------------|----------------|
   | Android | `content-desc` → `MobileBy.AccessibilityId()` | `app.Tap("automationId")` |
   | iOS | `name`/`label` → `MobileBy.AccessibilityId()` | `app.Tap("automationId")` |
   | Windows | `AutomationId` → `MobileBy.AccessibilityId()` | `app.Click("automationId")` |
   | macOS | `identifier` → `MobileBy.AccessibilityId()` | `app.Click("automationId")` |

4. **Determine affected platforms** from the PR diff (`#if ANDROID/IOS/WINDOWS/MACOS` guards, platform mentions). Default: all 4 platforms.

5. **Create structured bug analysis** per PR and **append to `doc/crbugs.md`**:
   ```
   ### Bug Analysis

   | Field | Value |
   |-------|-------|
   | Bug ID | {BugId} |
   | Control | SfAccordion |
   | Control Namespace | Syncfusion.Maui.Expander |
   | NuGet Package | Syncfusion.Maui.Expander |
   | Platforms | Android, iOS, Windows, macOS |
   | Bug | {ShortDescription} |
   | Root Cause | {RootCause} |
   | Fix | {SolutionDescription} |
   | Breaking | Yes/No |
   | Test Strategy | {How to reproduce and verify via Appium} |
   | AutomationId Pattern | {datagrid, column_N, cell_R_C, etc.} |
   | Element Finding Strategy | AccessibilityId (primary), XPath (fallback) |
   ```

---

### Phase 3: Automation Setup

1. **Locate the test sample** — The sample project is `AccordionCRBugsTestBed` at:
   ```
   UITest/Appium/AccordionCRBugsTestBed
   ```
   Check if this directory exists. If it does **not** exist:
   - **Read the `appium-project-creation` skill:**
     ```
     read_file .github/skills/appium-project-creation/SKILL.md
     ```
   - Scaffold a new Appium test project from the template at `.github/projecttemplate/SampleProject/`
   - Rename to `AccordionCRBugsTestBed` with:
     - `AppId`: `com.companyname.accordioncrbugs`
     - `AppName`: `AccordionCRBugsTestBed`
     - NuGet: `Syncfusion.Maui.Expander`
     - Namespace: `AccordionCRBugsTestBed`

2. **If the sample already exists**, inspect its structure:
   - Check `BaseTest.cs` for app identifiers
   - Check `UITests.Shared/Test/` for existing test classes
   - Check `MainPage.xaml.cs` for the navigation switch-case pattern
   - Check `MauiProgram.cs` for Syncfusion handler registration

3. **Pull latest and create feature branch:**
   ```bash
   git pull origin development
   git checkout -b automation/Bug_{BugId}
   ```
   If automating multiple bugs, use: `automation/CRBugs_Automation_{YYYY-MM-DD}`

---

### Phase 4: Sample and Test Case Creation

**Read these skills before proceeding:**
```
read_file .github/skills/bugsample-creation/SKILL.md
read_file .github/skills/appium-helper-extensions/SKILL.md
```

For **each** analyzed bug:

#### 4.1: Create Bug Reproduction XAML Page — `Bug_{BugId}.xaml`

```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             xmlns:sf="clr-namespace:Syncfusion.Maui.Expander;assembly=Syncfusion.Maui.Expander"
             x:Class="AccordionCRBugsTestBed.Bug_{BugId}"
             Title="Bug_{BugId}">
    <VerticalStackLayout Padding="10" Spacing="10">
        <Label Text="Bug #{BugId}: {ShortDescription}"
               AutomationId="bugTitle" FontSize="16" FontAttributes="Bold" />
        <sf:SfAccordion AutomationId="accordion"
                       {PropertiesForBugReproduction}>
            <!-- Columns and configuration to reproduce the bug -->
        </sf:SfAccordion>
        <Label AutomationId="statusLabel" Text="Status: Ready" />
    </VerticalStackLayout>
</ContentPage>
```

- Set `AutomationId` on **every** interactive element.
- Configure the control properties to **reproduce the specific bug scenario** from the PR diff and description.
- Add required data bindings, event handlers, and ViewModel if necessary.

#### 4.2: Create Code-Behind — `Bug_{BugId}.xaml.cs`

```csharp
namespace AccordionCRBugsTestBed;

/// <summary>
/// Bug #{BugId}: {BugDescription}
/// Root Cause: {RootCause}
/// Fix: {SolutionDescription}
/// </summary>
public partial class Bug_{BugId} : ContentPage
{
    public Bug_{BugId}()
    {
        InitializeComponent();
        // Setup BindingContext, data sources, event handlers as needed
    }
}
```

#### 4.3: Add Navigation Entry in `MainPage.xaml.cs`

Add a case to the navigation switch statement:
```csharp
case "Bug_{BugId}":
    await Navigation.PushAsync(new Bug_{BugId}());
    break;
```

#### 4.4: Write Appium Test Class — `UITests.Shared/Test/Bug_{BugId}Tests.cs`

```csharp
using NUnit.Framework;
using Syncfusion.UITestHelpers.Appium;
using Syncfusion.UITestHelpers.Core;
using UITests.Shared;

namespace AccordionCRBugsScripts
{
    public class Bug_{BugId}Tests : BaseTest
    {
        public Bug_{BugId}Tests(TestDevice testDevice) : base(testDevice) { }

        [SetUp]
        public void Setup()
        {
#if MACOS
            App.EnterFullScreen();
#endif
        }

        [TearDown]
        public void TearDown()
        {
#if MACOS
            App.ExitFullScreen();
#endif
            Reset();
        }

        [Test]
        [Description("Bug_{BugId}: {BugDescription}")]
        public void Bug_{BugId}_1()
        {
            // Navigate to the bug reproduction page
            Basicsbutton("Bug_{BugId}");
            Thread.Sleep(2000);

            // Verify the control loads correctly
            App.WaitForElement("accordion");

            // Reproduce the bug scenario using platform-specific helpers
            // {Insert reproduction steps derived from PR diff + bug description}

            // Capture screenshot for visual regression
            TakeAndCompareScreenshot("Bug_{BugId}_1");
        }
    }
}
```

#### 4.5: Platform-Specific Helper Method Reference

Use the correct helper methods per platform (from `appium-helper-extensions` skill):

| Action | Android | iOS | Windows | macOS |
|--------|---------|-----|---------|-------|
| Tap | `app.Tap("id")` | `app.Tap("id")` | `app.Click("id")` | `app.Click("id")` |
| Enter text | `app.EnterText("id", "text")` | `app.EnterTextiOS("id", "text")` | `app.EnterText("id", "text")` | `app.EnterText("id", "text")` |
| Dismiss keyboard | `app.DismissKeyboard()` | `app.iOSDone()` | `app.PressEnterWindows()` | N/A |
| Scroll down | `app.ScrollDownTo("t", "c")` | same | same | same |
| Orientation | `app.SetOrientationLandscape()` | same | N/A | N/A |
| Theme switch | `app.AndroidThemeChangeAction("dark")` | `app.iOSThemeChangeAction("dark")` | `app.WindowsThemeChangeAction("dark")` | `app.MacThemeChangeAction("dark")` |
| Screenshot | `TakeAndCompareScreenshot("n")` | same | same | same |
| Full screen | N/A | N/A | N/A | `app.EnterFullScreen()` / `app.ExitFullScreen()` |
| Wait | `app.WaitForElement("id")` | same | same | same |
| Exists check | `app.DoesElementExist("id")` | same | same | same |

Use `#if ANDROID`, `#if IOS`, `#if WINDOWS`, `#if MACOS` preprocessor directives for platform-specific test logic.

#### 4.6: Common Bug Reproduction Patterns

| Bug Type | Test Pattern |
|----------|-------------|
| Orientation bug | `SetOrientationLandscape()` → verify → `SetOrientationPortrait()` |
| Theme change bug | `AndroidThemeChangeAction("dark")` → verify → switch back |
| Keyboard interaction | `EnterText()` → `DismissKeyboard()` → verify layout |
| Scroll/visibility bug | `ScrollDownTo()` → `WaitForElement()` → screenshot |
| RTL layout bug | Set `FlowDirection="RightToLeft"` in XAML → verify layout |
| Data binding bug | Bind data → interact → verify bound values |
| Crash/NRE bug | Trigger crash action → verify no exception + screenshot |
| Column resize/reorder | Drag column → verify → screenshot |
| Sorting/grouping bug | Tap column header → verify sort → screenshot |
| Filtering bug | Apply filter → verify filtered data → screenshot |
| Selection bug | Tap row/cell → verify selection state → screenshot |
| Editing bug | Double-tap cell → edit → commit → verify → screenshot |

